1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,753
Creech Manor: over a hundred years old, full of historic charm, and every room has a

2
00:00:04,753 --> 00:00:05,655
horrifying story.

3
00:00:05,875 --> 00:00:07,624
Here's how the location plays.

4
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:12,871
Creech Manor has no special setup, but the house itself has a few rules of its own.

5
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:17,823
Creech Manor has three one-way spaces. White arrows and lines show the only

6
00:00:17,823 --> 00:00:19,417
direction you can leave them.

7
00:00:19,637 --> 00:00:23,203
You can't move against an arrow. So you can't climb up the tyre swing and back in

8
00:00:23,203 --> 00:00:26,857
through the window, and you can't climb up through the hole in the washroom ceiling

9
00:00:26,857 --> 00:00:27,957
on the left of the board.

10
00:00:28,177 --> 00:00:30,384
Victims and Enemies follow the same rule.

11
00:00:30,384 --> 00:00:34,852
But the spaces still count as adjacent in both directions, for attacks and anything

12
00:00:34,852 --> 00:00:36,305
else that checks adjacency.

13
00:00:36,525 --> 00:00:38,909
The one exception is the Rope Ladder item.

14
00:00:38,909 --> 00:00:42,541
Once used, it turns a one-way space into a normal two-way space.

15
00:00:43,367 --> 00:00:45,511
Window spaces are marked with a window icon.

16
00:00:45,511 --> 00:00:48,679
There are two on the right side of the house and one on the left.

17
00:00:48,899 --> 00:00:53,168
They have no rules of their own, but many Terror and Event cards target them, for

18
00:00:53,168 --> 00:00:56,594
example sending panicking Victims out of a window to their death.

19
00:00:56,594 --> 00:00:58,755
So keep an eye on who is standing by one.

20
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:03,368
Whenever a card mentions The Ladder, it means the ladder on the outside of the

21
00:01:03,368 --> 00:01:06,585
building, joining the left exit space to the third-floor washroom.

22
00:01:06,805 --> 00:01:09,497
The ladder drawn up to the attic is just artwork.

23
00:01:09,497 --> 00:01:11,200
No game effect ever touches it.

24
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:16,364
Every space counts as Inside, except the three exit spaces, which are Outside.

25
00:01:16,584 --> 00:01:20,408
Several cards check this. For example, when the windows and doors slam shut:

26
00:01:20,408 --> 00:01:23,578
if you're Inside, you can't move during your next Action phase;

27
00:01:23,578 --> 00:01:25,843
if you're Outside, you can't enter the house.

28
00:01:26,063 --> 00:01:30,193
And the Lights Out event makes you roll one fewer die whenever an Action card lets

29
00:01:30,193 --> 00:01:32,761
you move, unless you have a Flashlight or a Candle.

30
00:01:33,567 --> 00:01:37,300
A few tips. The exits are at street level, so bring Victims down early.

31
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:40,613
Avoid the Attic: Victims sent there tend to die in bulk.

32
00:01:40,833 --> 00:01:44,097
If Lights Out comes up, a Flashlight or Candle keeps you moving.

33
00:01:44,317 --> 00:01:48,492
It's one of the tougher locations, especially against the Poltergeist and the Birds.

34
00:01:48,492 --> 00:01:48,989
Good luck.

